#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:1
msgid "Serving a Nix store via HTTP"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:3
msgid ""
"You can easily share the Nix store of a machine via HTTP. This allows other "
"machines to fetch store paths from that machine to speed up installations. "
"It uses the same _binary cache_ mechanism that Nix usually uses to fetch pre-"
"built binaries from <https://cache.nixos.org>."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:8
msgid ""
"The daemon that handles binary cache requests via HTTP, `nix-serve`, is not "
"part of the Nix distribution, but you can install it from Nixpkgs:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:15
msgid ""
"You can then start the server, listening for HTTP connections on whatever "
"port you like:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:22
msgid ""
"To check whether it works, try fetching the [`nix-cache-info`](../protocols/"
"binary-cache/nix-cache-info.md) file on the client:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:24
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ curl http://avalon:8080/nix-cache-info\n"
"StoreDir: /nix/store\n"
"WantMassQuery: 1\n"
"Priority: 30\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:31
msgid ""
"When writing to a binary cache (e.g., with [`nix copy`](../command-ref/new-"
"cli/nix3-copy.md)), Nix creates [`nix-cache-info`](../protocols/binary-cache/"
"nix-cache-info.md) automatically if it doesn't exist."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:33
msgid ""
"On the client side, you can tell Nix to use your binary cache using `--"
"substituters`, e.g.:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:36
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ nix-env --install --attr nixpkgs.firefox --substituters http://"
"avalon:8080/\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:40
msgid ""
"The option `substituters` tells Nix to use this binary cache in addition to "
"your default caches, such as <https://cache.nixos.org>. Thus, for any path "
"in the closure of Firefox, Nix will first check if the path is available on "
"the server `avalon` or another binary caches. If not, it will fall back to "
"building from source."
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:46
msgid ""
"You can also tell Nix to always use your binary cache by adding a line to "
"the `nix.conf` configuration file like this:"
msgstr ""

#: source/package-management/binary-cache-substituter.md:49
msgid ""
"    substituters = http://avalon:8080/ https://cache.nixos.org/\n"
"    "
msgstr ""
